**assistant**:
> Function templates generally must be **defined in the header**, because each translation unit that calls them needs to instantiate the specialization (e.g. `streamInsertVector<HydroOutputNode>`).
> 
> `SerializationTools.cpp` compiles the template definitions, but it does not itself instantiate them for `HydroOutputNode`, so no matching symbols are emitted for the linker.
> 
> ### Recommended fix: move definitions into the header
> 
> Put the definitions in `SerializationTools.h` (or in a `.tpp`/`.ipp` file included at the end of the header).
> 
> Also fix two issues in the implementations:
> 
> ```cpp
> template <class T>
> std::ostream& streamInsertVector(
>     std::vector<T*>& vec,
>     std::ostream& os,
>     PointerTracker& tracker)
> {
>     os << vec.size() << " ";
> 
>     for (T* item : vec) {
>         item->streamInsertPointer(os, tracker);
>     }
> 
>     return os;
> }
> 
> template <class T>
> std::istream& streamExtractVector(
>     std::istream& in,
>     PointerReference& reference,
>     std::vector<T*>& vec,
>     void* (*constructor)(std::istream&, PointerReference&))
> {
>     unsigned count;
>     in >> count;
> 
>     vec.clear();
> 
>     for (unsigned ii = 0; ii < count; ++ii) {
>         T* item = static_cast<T*>(
>             reference.streamExtractPointer(in, constructor)
>         );
>         vec.push_back(item);  // not vec.insert(item)
>     }
> 
>     return in;
> }
> ```
> 
> Your original code has these additional problems:
> 
> - `vector<IPointerSerializable*>::const_iterator` cannot iterate over a `vector<T*>`; vectors are invariant. Use `T*`, `auto`, or `vector<T*>::const_iterator`.
> - `std::vector` has no `insert(item)` overload that appends an item. Use `push_back(item)`.
> 
> ### Alternative: explicit instantiation
> 
> If you deliberately want definitions in the `.cpp`, explicitly instantiate every used specialization there:
> 
> ```cpp
> template std::ostream& streamInsertVector<HydroOutputNode>(
>     std::vector<HydroOutputNode*>&,
>     std::ostream&,
>     PointerTracker&
> );
> 
> template std::istream& streamExtractVector<HydroOutputNode>(
>     std::istream&,
>     PointerReference&,
>     std::vector<HydroOutputNode*>&,
>     void* (*)(std::istream&, PointerReference&)
> );
> ```
> 
> But this requires including the complete definition of `HydroOutputNode` in `SerializationTools.cpp`, and doing this for every `T`. Header-defined templates are usually the better choice.
